<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Fossestien — Full marked Gaularfjellet–Eldal Fossestien walking main [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Walk the full marked Fossestien route from Gaularfjellet/Torsnesstølen through Longestølen and Likholefossen to the western river-path finish at Eldal. Follow red F marks through forest, bridges and summer-pasture land, including the narrow lower gorge. Plan roughly 18.8 km and about seven hours plus stops; climbing estimates are approximate. Arrange return transport and confirm pickup locations; the paid Hov shuttle needs booking by the previous day. Choose dry, snow-free conditions, watch for slippery bridges and river hazards, close gates, respect livestock and keep dogs leashed as requested. This is a walking route; obey closures.

Approximate 540 m ascent and 920 m descent are historical 10 m terrain/API estimates, using bilinear samples on the complete route and centred 25 m sample-mean smoothing, rounded to 10 m. Smoothing sensitivity is substantial: 50 m smoothing gives about 450 m ascent / 830 m descent, and 100 m gives about 360 m / 750 m — roughly 90–180 m variation around the 25 m estimate. Terrain age, local error and density-weighted sampling add uncertainty. These are planning estimates, not field/GPS measurements, direct publisher measurements or a precise current elevation profile. No point heights or vertical datum are claimed. The earlier 220 m ascent and the publisher’s 500 m altitude difference are not used as total-descent estimates. Inherited 420 minutes remains an approximate planning duration; allow additional time for footing, weather and stops.

Route geometry: © Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; TurOgFriluftsruter / Nasjonal database for turruter, released municipal Sunnfjord and Sogndal walking GML records maintained by Hov Hyttegrend. Creative Commons Attribution 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Source: https://nedlasting.geonorge.no/geonorge/Friluftsliv/TurOgFriluftsruter/GML/Friluftsliv_4647_Sunnfjord_25832_TurOgFriluftsruter_GML.zip; https://nedlasting.geonorge.no/geonorge/Friluftsliv/TurOgFriluftsruter/GML/Friluftsliv_4640_Sogndal_25832_TurOgFriluftsruter_GML.zip. Changes: full-precision EPSG25832 to WGS84/EPSG4326 transformation with always_xy, 62 ordered archive/GML-identified record traversals (61 distinct local IDs), direction reversal where required and duplicate shared-junction removal only; every original municipal-border position and edge is retained. All 4,366 positions derive from original released walking records; canonical display uses the existing source vertex simplifier. No snapping, synthetic joins, farm-centroid welding, OSM/operator coordinate donation or invented elevations. Two-dimensional planning geometry, not navigation-grade or an access permit. Approximate metric source: © Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; DTM10 Terrengmodell UTM33, historical source2102 / 6800_3_10m_z33, CC BY 4.0 https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Terrain/API sampling, centred smoothing and rounding changes are described above. Terrain supplies metric facts only and contributes no public route coordinates or height profile.

